EzScenarioPython

This product includes a Python port derived from ezSpec, originally developed
by Teddy Chen and the ezKanban Team.

Original project: https://gitlab.com/TeddyChen/ezspec
Original artifact family: tw.teddysoft.ezspec:ezspec-core
Reference source commit: 061eadc8dd47510bf12d62dd87d3fdaa0a37b20d
Reference root pom.xml revision: 2.0.5

This independently maintained adaptation translates the developer-facing DSL
to Python, replaces JUnit integration with pytest, adds collection-time
Scenario Outline examples and per-row execution, and implements Python TXT
and JSON reporting. It is not a release published by the upstream ezSpec team.

